<!-- OstrichChallenge: NO ZOMBIE BEARS, NO BEARS, NO DIRE WOLVES

     Fril: "Rears both normal and zombie must be removed from the Wasteland with dire wolves,
     we do this in hospital."

     ================================================================================
     HE WAS RIGHT AND I WAS WRONG, TWICE OVER. THIS IS HIS CODE, NOT MINE.
     ================================================================================
     v1.15.1 of this file was my own work, written after reading the Hospital DEVLOG and
     finding the removal listed as an open TBD in two places (lines 503 and 1197, neither
     struck through). I told Fril the Hospital had never done it.

     Fril: "Ive played and seen played Hospital in the wasteland many times and Ive never seen
     a direwolf or zombie bear. As far as I was concerned they had been removed."

     He then sent the Hospital's actual entitygroups.xml and the three lines below are in it,
     verbatim. THE HOSPITAL DEVLOG IS OUT OF DATE; the change shipped and the TBD was never
     struck through. His memory of his own mod beat the document about it, and it beat my
     reading of that document.

     THE LESSON, and it is the inverse of the one I wrote last night: "check the artefact, not
     the memory" is only half a rule. A devlog IS a memory, just a written one, and a stale
     entry reads exactly like a current one. The artefact that settles a question about what
     CODE does is the CODE. I had the devlog and treated it as the artefact.

     ================================================================================
     WHY HIS THREE LINES ARE BETTER THAN MY FIVE
     ================================================================================
     v1.15.1 zeroed five @p attributes across the three Wasteland-named groups. This removes
     the entries outright, everywhere in the game, and it is better in three ways:

       GLOBAL         Every group, not just the wasteland. That catches the seventy-plus
                      feralHordeStageGS* groups carrying animalDireWolf at 0.1, which my
                      version left alone and flagged as an open question. It also catches
                      ZombiesDowntown, ZombiesForestDowntown, EnemyAnimalsSnow and the rest.

       SELF-GROUPS    The not() guards keep the dedicated single-animal groups intact:
                      animalZombieBear, ZombieBearsGroup, animalDireWolf, animalBear,
                      animalBearSmall, BearGroup, BearSmallGroup. Anything that deliberately
                      spawns one — a quest, an SVS script, a console spawn — still works.
                      Only the mixed pools lose them.

       animalBear     My version wrote nothing for the normal bear because it appears in no
                      Wasteland group. Fril asked for it and his line covers it wherever it
                      is, which is the request rather than my narrowing of it.

     His file also records the bug behind the exact @n matching: the old form used
     contains(text(), 'animalBear'), which also caught animalBearSmall.

     ================================================================================
     THE COMPANION PATCH IS NOT OPTIONAL
     ================================================================================
     EnemyAnimalsWastelandNight is dire wolf 20, zombie bear 20, none 60. Removing both
     animals leaves a group whose only entry is "none", and EntityGroups.IsEnemyGroup ends

         return EntityClass.list[list[0].entityClassId].bIsEnemyEntity;

     with no guard on that lookup. It null-checks the list and checks Count >= 1, so an EMPTY
     group is safe, but a group holding only "none" has Count 1 and an unresolvable class id,
     and EntityClass.list[-1] returns null. That throws every tick.

     That is why the Hospital also ships HospitalIsEnemyGroupPatch, and why this mod now ships
     the same guard as EntityGroups_IsEnemyGroup_Patch in Animals.cs. The two pieces go
     together: DO NOT take these three lines without it.
-->
<configs>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         ANIMAL REMOVALS — copied from the Hospital's entitygroups.xml, unchanged.
         Exact @n matching; the group-name guards keep the dedicated
         single-animal groups working.
    ===================================================================== -->

    <remove xpath="//entitygroup[not(@name='animalZombieBear') and not(@name='ZombieBearsGroup')]/e[@n='animalZombieBear']"/>
    <remove xpath="//entitygroup[not(@name='animalDireWolf')]/e[@n='animalDireWolf']"/>
    <remove xpath="//entitygroup[not(@name='animalBear') and not(@name='animalBearSmall') and not(@name='BearGroup') and not(@name='BearSmallGroup')]/e[@n='animalBear']"/>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         NO SCREAMERS, ANYWHERE (v1.235.0)

         Fril, 11 Nov: "Can we remove all screamers from spawning in Hordes", and when told
         they were already absent from every horde list vanilla ships: "Yes, gone from the
         game. Remove them from the heat system and only keep regular zombies in that".

         WHAT WAS CHECKED FIRST, because his first request was already true. Vanilla 3.4 has
         1875 entitygroups. With comments stripped, exactly SEVEN contain a screamer: the
         three ZombieScouts groups below and four single-entity self-groups. Every
         feralHordeStageGS (322 of them), wanderingHordeStageGS (19), badassHordeStageGS (55),
         sleeperHordeStageGS (322), defenseHordeStageGS (322) and policeCarHordeStageGS (55)
         has none. TFP even commented the screamers out of scoutHordeStageGS, which is the
         horde a screamer calls in. A first pass that counted commented-out lines said 124
         groups and was wrong; the number is seven.

         So the screamer only ever reaches the world through the chunk heat map, and these
         three groups are the whole of it:

             heat >= 25 on a chunk  ->  AIDirectorChunkEventComponent.SpawnScouts
             gamestage  < 45  Scouts1        ->  ZombieScouts
             gamestage  < 85  Scouts2        ->  ZombieScouts
             gamestage  < 125 ScoutsFeral    ->  ZombieScoutsFeral
             gamestage >= 125 ScoutsRadiated ->  ZombieScoutsRadiated

         THE COMPANION PATCH IS NOT OPTIONAL, and this is the whole reason src/Scouts.cs
         exists. There is no screamer in the game's CODE: one search of the entire assembly
         for "Screamer" returns a single log string. The horde-calling is attached to the
         SLOT, not to the zombie, and the scout chain never asks what kind of zombie it was
         handed. Swapping these entries without the patch would give a regular zombie that
         still summons a horde, with no scream and no distinctive model to warn you it is
         happening: the tell lost and the horde kept. Scouts.cs refuses the horde call, and
         vanilla's own branch then releases the zombie to carry on as an ordinary one.

         DO NOT TAKE THESE LINES WITHOUT src/Scouts.cs.

         ELEVEN REPLACEMENTS, TIERED TO MATCH WHAT THE SLOT USED TO SEND. The base eleven go
         in ZombieScouts, their Feral twins in ZombieScoutsFeral and their Radiated twins in
         ZombieScoutsRadiated, so a gamestage 150 scout is still a gamestage 150 problem. All
         thirty-three class names were resolved against the game's own entityclasses.xml
         before shipping, and none of them is on Fril's v1.15.0 exclusion list (Screamer,
         FatCop, Chuck, Spider, PlagueSpitter, Rancher, Mutated) or is the stalker.

         APPEND BEFORE REMOVE, deliberately. Each group holds exactly one entry, the screamer.
         Removing first would leave it momentarily empty. EntityGroups.IsEnemyGroup does guard
         an empty list (see the note above and Animals.cs), so this is belt and braces rather
         than a known fault, but it costs nothing to never create the state.

         THE SELF-GROUPS ARE LEFT ALONE ON PURPOSE, exactly as the animal removals above leave
         animalZombieBear and the rest intact: zombieScreamer, zombieScreamerFeral,
         zombieScreamerRadiated, zombieScreamerCharged and zombieScreamerInfernal still exist
         and still hold her. Nothing spawns from them on its own, so a quest, an SVS script or
         a console spawn still works. Screamers are gone from the game as it plays, not deleted
         from it.
    ===================================================================== -->

    <append xpath="//entitygroup[@name='ZombieScouts']">
        <e n="zombieArlene"/>
        <e n="zombieBoe"/>
        <e n="zombieDarlene"/>
        <e n="zombieJoe"/>
        <e n="zombieMarlene"/>
        <e n="zombieSteve"/>
        <e n="zombieYo"/>
        <e n="zombieBusinessMan"/>
        <e n="zombieNurse"/>
        <e n="zombieUtilityWorker"/>
        <e n="zombieTomClark"/>
    </append>
    <remove xpath="//entitygroup[@name='ZombieScouts']/e[@n='zombieScreamer']"/>

    <append xpath="//entitygroup[@name='ZombieScoutsFeral']">
        <e n="zombieArleneFeral"/>
        <e n="zombieBoeFeral"/>
        <e n="zombieDarleneFeral"/>
        <e n="zombieJoeFeral"/>
        <e n="zombieMarleneFeral"/>
        <e n="zombieSteveFeral"/>
        <e n="zombieYoFeral"/>
        <e n="zombieBusinessManFeral"/>
        <e n="zombieNurseFeral"/>
        <e n="zombieUtilityWorkerFeral"/>
        <e n="zombieTomClarkFeral"/>
    </append>
    <remove xpath="//entitygroup[@name='ZombieScoutsFeral']/e[@n='zombieScreamerFeral']"/>

    <append xpath="//entitygroup[@name='ZombieScoutsRadiated']">
        <e n="zombieArleneRadiated"/>
        <e n="zombieBoeRadiated"/>
        <e n="zombieDarleneRadiated"/>
        <e n="zombieJoeRadiated"/>
        <e n="zombieMarleneRadiated"/>
        <e n="zombieSteveRadiated"/>
        <e n="zombieYoRadiated"/>
        <e n="zombieBusinessManRadiated"/>
        <e n="zombieNurseRadiated"/>
        <e n="zombieUtilityWorkerRadiated"/>
        <e n="zombieTomClarkRadiated"/>
    </append>
    <remove xpath="//entitygroup[@name='ZombieScoutsRadiated']/e[@n='zombieScreamerRadiated']"/>

</configs>
